!!! Access and error logs.
!!!
!!! A server you cannot see is a server you cannot operate: no way to know
!!! which request 500'd, which client is hammering a route, or whether the
!!! thing is serving at all. This writes the two logs every other server
!!! writes, in the format every log reader already parses.
!!!
!!! The access log is the Combined Log Format, which is Apache's and nginx's:
!!!
!!!   127.0.0.1 - - [10/Oct/2000:13:55:36 +0000] "GET /x HTTP/1.1" 200 2326 "-" "curl/8"
!!!
!!! Not a format of our own. Anything that reads a web server's logs — GoAccess,
!!! an ELK pipeline, awk — already reads this one, and a new format would mean
!!! every one of those needed teaching.
!!!
!!! BUFFERED, AND WHY.
!!!
!!! nil.std.io's only appending call is `append_text`, which opens, writes and
!!! closes. Per request that is three syscalls on the hot path, and the handle
!!! API that would avoid them is private and takes raw byte buffers a Matrix
!!! page cannot build. So lines are held and written in batches.
!!!
!!! The server flushes when it has nothing to serve, which it already detects
!!! each pass. Logging then costs nothing under load and an idle server has an
!!! up-to-date log — the two things that matter, in the order they matter. A
!!! ceiling forces a flush as well, so sustained load cannot grow the buffer
!!! without bound.
!!!
!!! What this costs is a window: lines buffered when the process dies are
!!! lost. That is the trade `append_text` imposes, it is stated here rather
!!! than discovered, and `flush-now` is available to anything that would
!!! rather pay the syscalls.

book nilweb.log.access

read nil.std.core
read nil.std.io.file
read nil.std.text
read nil.std.text.string_utils
read everything from nilweb.time.clock
read everything from nilweb.text.scan
read everything from nilweb.http.method
read everything from nilweb.http.headers
read everything from nilweb.http.request


!!! Lines held before a flush is forced regardless of whether the server is
!!! busy. Low enough that a crash loses little, high enough that a loaded
!!! server is not opening the file every few requests.
constant buffer-limit as number is 64


public variable access-path as text is ""
public variable error-path as text is ""
public variable access-buffer as array of text is []
public variable error-buffer as array of text is []
!!! Lines dropped because the log could not be written. Counted rather than
!!! reported per line: a log that cannot be written must not turn every
!!! request into a second failure, but silence about it would be worse.
public variable dropped-lines as number is 0

!!! The last formatted log stamp, and the second it belongs to.
!!!
!!! Formatting one means the full calendar conversion, and at a few hundred
!!! requests a second the answer is the same for hundreds of them in a row.
!!! Keyed on the epoch second because that is the resolution the format has.
!!!
!!! Also did not show as a throughput gain when measured. Logging costs about
!!! a fifth of the request rate and neither this nor the scan above is where
!!! it goes; that is still unaccounted for and recorded as such in the README
!!! rather than attributed to a guess.
variable stamp-second as number is 0 minus 1
variable stamp-text as text is ""


stamp-for receives at-ms as number returns text begin paragraph
    value second-of is at-ms over 1000
    when second-of equals nilweb.log.access::stamp-second then
        give nilweb.log.access::stamp-text
    end when
    value formatted is log-date with at-ms being at-ms
    set nilweb.log.access::stamp-second to second-of
    set nilweb.log.access::stamp-text to formatted
    give formatted
end paragraph


!!! --- Where the logs go. An empty path means that log is off.
!!!
!!! Off by default. A framework that starts writing files into whatever
!!! directory it was launched from, without being asked, is a framework that
!!! fills a disk on someone's laptop.

public log-to receives access-file as text, error-file as text returns nothing begin paragraph
    set nilweb.log.access::access-path to access-file
    set nilweb.log.access::error-path to error-file
    give nothing
end paragraph


public logging-access returns boolean begin paragraph
    give not (nilweb.log.access::access-path equals "")
end paragraph


public buffered-count returns number begin paragraph
    give (the length of nilweb.log.access::access-buffer)
        plus (the length of nilweb.log.access::error-buffer)
end paragraph


public dropped-count returns number begin paragraph
    give nilweb.log.access::dropped-lines
end paragraph


!!! --- Record one served request.
!!!
!!! `bytes` is the body's length and not the whole response, because that is
!!! what the format means and what every reader summing the column expects.
!!! A request that produced no body logs 0 rather than "-"; both are seen in
!!! the wild and a number is easier to sum.

public record-request receives client as text, request as http-request, code as number,
    bytes as number, at-ms as number returns nothing begin paragraph
    when not (logging-access with nothing) then
        give nothing
    end when

    value line is (shown with raw being client) plus " - - ["
        plus (stamp-for with at-ms being at-ms) plus "] "
        plus quote plus (request-line-of with request being request) plus quote plus " "
        plus (code becomes text) plus " " plus (bytes becomes text) plus " "
        plus quote plus (shown with raw being (header-of with request being request, name being "Referer")) plus quote plus " "
        plus quote plus (shown with raw being (header-of with request being request, name being "User-Agent")) plus quote
    append line to nilweb.log.access::access-buffer
    when (the length of nilweb.log.access::access-buffer) is at least buffer-limit then
        evaluate flush-now with nothing
    end when
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- Record a request that could not be parsed.
!!! Logged with a dash where the request line would be, because there is no
!!! request line: logging the raw bytes would put attacker-controlled text
!!! into the log, which is how a log viewer becomes the vulnerability.

public record-malformed receives client as text, code as number, at-ms as number returns nothing begin paragraph
    when not (logging-access with nothing) then
        give nothing
    end when
    append (shown with raw being client) plus " - - ["
        plus (stamp-for with at-ms being at-ms) plus "] " plus quote plus "-" plus quote plus " "
        plus (code becomes text) plus " 0 " plus quote plus "-" plus quote plus " " plus quote plus "-" plus quote
        to nilweb.log.access::access-buffer
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- Record something the operator needs to know.
!!! One line, an ISO instant first so the file sorts in time order.

public record-error receives severity as text, message as text, at-ms as number returns nothing begin paragraph
    when nilweb.log.access::error-path equals "" then
        give nothing
    end when
    append (iso-instant with at-ms being at-ms) plus " [" plus severity plus "] "
        plus (one-line with raw being message) to nilweb.log.access::error-buffer
    when (the length of nilweb.log.access::error-buffer) is at least buffer-limit then
        evaluate flush-now with nothing
    end when
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- Write everything held. Called by the server when it has nothing to
!!! serve, and by the buffer ceiling.

public flush-now returns nothing begin paragraph
    evaluate flush-one with path being nilweb.log.access::access-path, which being "access"
    evaluate flush-one with path being nilweb.log.access::error-path, which being "error"
    give nothing
end paragraph


flush-one receives path as text, which as text returns nothing begin paragraph
    value lines is when which equals "access"
        give nilweb.log.access::access-buffer
        otherwise give nilweb.log.access::error-buffer
    end when
    when path equals "" or (the length of lines) equals 0 then
        give nothing
    end when

    variable block as text is ""
    repeat for each line in lines
        set block to block plus line plus newline
    end repeat

    !!! Cleared before the write, not after. A write that fails must not leave
    !!! the lines queued for the next attempt: the next attempt will fail the
    !!! same way, the buffer grows without bound, and a full disk becomes an
    !!! out-of-memory. They are counted instead.
    value held is the length of lines
    evaluate clear-one with which being which

    value written is nil.std.io::append_text with path being path, content being block
    consider written
        when Result.Ok holding done then give nothing
        otherwise set nilweb.log.access::dropped-lines to nilweb.log.access::dropped-lines plus held
    end consider
    give nothing
end paragraph


clear-one receives which as text returns nothing begin paragraph
    variable empty as array of text is []
    when which equals "access" then
        set nilweb.log.access::access-buffer to empty
    otherwise
        set nilweb.log.access::error-buffer to empty
    end when
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- The request line, rebuilt rather than kept.
!!! From the parsed parts, so what is logged is what the server acted on. A
!!! log of the raw line would record what the client sent, which is the more
!!! honest thing to log and also attacker-controlled; this records the
!!! decision, and record-malformed covers the case where there was none.

request-line-of receives request as http-request returns text begin paragraph
    give (method-name with verb being request.verb) plus " "
        plus (one-line with raw being request.target) plus " " plus request.version
end paragraph


!!! --- A field value for a log line, or "-" when it is absent.

shown receives raw as text returns text begin paragraph
    value cleaned is one-line with raw being raw
    give when cleaned equals "" give "-" otherwise give cleaned end when
end paragraph


!!! --- Strip what would break the format or forge a line.
!!!
!!! A header value is attacker-controlled. A newline in it would end the log
!!! line and start one of the attacker's choosing — a forged entry in a file
!!! someone will later read as evidence. A quote would close the quoted field
!!! early and do the same to a parser. Both are replaced rather than escaped,
!!! because every reader of this format already handles neither.
!!!
!!! A control byte is dropped too: a log read in a terminal should not be able
!!! to move the cursor or set a colour.

public one-line receives raw as text returns text begin paragraph
    !!! Scanned before it is rebuilt, and almost never rebuilt.
    !!!
    !!! Appending a byte at a time grows a new text on every step, so a
    !!! rebuild is quadratic in the length of the value. Nearly every header
    !!! is already clean, so the common path is a scan that allocates nothing
    !!! and gives the input back.
    !!!
    !!! This did NOT show up as a throughput gain when it was measured: 291
    !!! requests a second either way, because the values a benchmark sends are
    !!! short and the quadratic term never bites. It is kept for the long
    !!! values a real client sends -- a 150-character user-agent, a referer
    !!! with a query -- and not on the strength of a measurement it did not
    !!! earn.
    when not (needs-cleaning with raw being raw) then
        give nil.std.text::trim with s being raw
    end when

    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being raw
    variable out as text is ""
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than width
        value code is nil.std.text::byte_at with s being raw, index being index
        when byte-is-safe with code being code then
            set out to out plus (nil.std.text::from_byte with code being code)
        otherwise
            !!! One space per removed byte, so a value's length is not changed
            !!! by sanitising it and a reader cannot be misled about how long
            !!! the original was.
            set out to out plus " "
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give nil.std.text::trim with s being out
end paragraph


needs-cleaning receives raw as text returns boolean begin paragraph
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being raw
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than width
        when not (byte-is-safe with code being
            (nil.std.text::byte_at with s being raw, index being index)) then
            give true
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give false
end paragraph


!!! --- Whether a byte may appear in a log field.
!!!
!!! A quote would close a quoted field early and a backslash would be read as
!!! an escape by a parser expecting one; both let an attacker end a field. A
!!! newline ends the whole line and starts one of their choosing -- a forged
!!! entry in a file someone will read as evidence. A control byte can move a
!!! terminal's cursor or set a colour, and a log is read in a terminal.

byte-is-safe receives code as number returns boolean begin paragraph
    give code is at least 32 and code does not equal 127
        and code does not equal 34 and code does not equal 92
end paragraph
